A hardened implementation should assert these conditions at runtime: scheme is HTTPS, host parses cleanly, userinfo is absent, DNS answers exist, at least one IP is globally routable, the exact dialed IP is one of the vetted IPs, redirects are capped at 3, connect timeout is 5 seconds, read timeout is 30 seconds, body size stays under 10 MB, and the breaker remains closed before any external dial is attempted. For standards alignment, use OWASP SSRF guidance as the control baseline, RFC 4193 for IPv6 ULA classification, and Node.js TLS configuration docs for TLS 1.3 behavior and cipher naming.

A practical deployment rule is: **all egress is denied by default, and only a narrow, validated, audited, TLS-enforced path is permitted**. That is the fail-closed posture you want for GNW Production Closure.

