**Specification.** A readiness probe should confirm an actual database round trip, not only process liveness. Use a temporary probe row in a dedicated table, write it and read it back on the same transaction/connection, then roll back. This verifies active write/read capability without retaining probe records.

```sql
CREATE TABLE app.health_probe (
  nonce uuid PRIMARY KEY,
  checked_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, DELETE ON app.health_probe TO app_runtime;
```

